    <!--
        Toolbar icons, as vector paths.

        Source: Fluent UI System Icons by Microsoft, "Regular" style, MIT License
        (https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-system-icons) - the same set the
        BluePrint designer's own icons come from, so both look alike. The license
        text is in README.md.

        - The toolbar icons are 24 x 24 (coordinates 0..24) and the alignment
          icons 16 x 16. Draw them with the Bp.ToolIcon / Bp.SmallIcon styles
          below: Stretch="None" keeps the icon's own square, so a thin icon such
          as Line is not stretched to fill the button.
        - "F1" makes the fill rule nonzero, the default of SVG.
        - The fill is the button's Foreground, so the icons follow the light and
          dark themes and fade on a disabled button with no extra work.
        - 24 rather than the 16 of the BluePrint toolbars: this application has
          few buttons and is meant to be easy to read at a glance.
        - AlignTop / AlignMiddle / AlignBottom come from Textbox Align Top /
          Middle / Bottom with the box outline removed. Without the box, the two
          bars run the full width of the 16 x 16 square, as the Align Left /
          Center / Right lines do, and sit at its top, middle and bottom so the
          three buttons still tell apart.
    -->

